1
00:00:00,046 --> 00:00:11,920
What's happening right now is a big deal. This is the biggest launch since ChatGPT. It's called Muse. Muse. Muse. It has a tech world buzzing. 5 million downloads in 22 days. Surpassing ChatGPT.

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:21,520
And he built it. Most people are using AI to answer questions, basically glorified Google search. This is something totally different. It's an AI agent built for everyday life.

3
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:32,400
We believe that Muse will make you money. One guy had Muse help plan a weekend away with his wife. It can make phone calls, it can do tasks for you. But for it to work, you have to trust it.

4
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:41,360
First with your personal information, then to do what you actually want it to do, and then that it's not gonna, well, get out of control.

5
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:50,000
All at a time when the most important AI leaders are warning us that AI is getting out of control. And I urge you to urge me to stop.

6
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:57,840
If you understand what's happening right now with Muse, you'll understand the biggest things happening in AI. So, what can it actually do?

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:09,440
When should we trust it? And what do we need to do to make sure this goes right? And we're at the moment of like peak insanity. Why are all these billionaires obsessed with restaurant reservations?

